OL,3,GNEWSACity 'eyesores' could become      
OL,4,Ahundreds of new homes                  
OL,6,FProminent empty city centre buildings  
OL,7,Fwhich have long-been described as      
OL,8,F"eyesores" could be turned into        
OL,9,Fhundreds of new homes.                 
OL,11,FA total of 1,020 homes across 17 sites 
OL,12,Fin Gloucester have been earmarked by   
OL,13,Fthe city council for housing, including
OL,14,Flong-term empty buildings,             
OL,15,Funder-utilised land and car parks.     
OL,17,FThese include the former Wilko's and   
OL,18,FSpread Eagle Court on Northgate Street,
OL,19,Fwhich could be turned into a combined  
OL,20,F90 homes.                              
OL,23,APub: 21-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2 
